WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.802
-The president brought us
to the brink

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.471
of a disastrous war with Iran

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.772
and then today claimed credit
for stopping it.

00:00:06.772 --> 00:00:08.741
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:13.446 line:0%
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.581
Last night,
Iran launched missiles

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:17.917
at two bases in Iraq
housing US troops

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.086
in retaliation
for the assassination

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:23.088
of a top Iranian general,
Qasem Soleimani.

00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:24.924
It was obviously
a harrowing moment

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.393
with the lives of US and Iraqi
troops at risk,

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.362
and everyone had
that sickening feeling

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.297
that we maybe had just lurched

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.566
into an immoral and catastrophic
war with Iran.

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:35.434
It was one of those moments
where you're watching footage

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:38.271
of missiles streaking through
the night on CNN and you think,

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:41.207
"God, I hope we have smart
and steady leadership."

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.876
And then you say, "Oh, no."

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:46.645
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:49.749
Now, thankfully,
there were no casualties,

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.184
which was fantastic news
and a huge relief.

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:53.719
But Trump delivered that news
last night

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:54.788
with a very bizarre tweet.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:57.090
This was all we heard last night

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.958
from our commander-in-chief.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.693
-All is well.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.862
Missiles launched from Iran

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:06.365
at two military bases
located in Iraq.

00:01:06.365 --> 00:01:11.204
Assessment of casualties
and damages taking place now.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.471
So far, so good.

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:13.873
-"All is well"?

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.776
That's not how you address
the nation on matters of war.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.878
That's how a sophomore
addresses his parents

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.746
on a postcard
from a trip abroad.

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:22.882
[ Laughter ]
"Hello from Reykjavik!

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:25.217
It's cold here, and super
expensive for some reason.

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:26.419
Otherwise, all is well!"

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:27.720
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.889
Then, today, Trump followed up
on that tweet

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:32.392
and addressed the nation
in a rambling speech

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:35.628
in which he claimed credit
for ending a crisis he started,

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:37.530
bragged about US military might,

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.033
announced crushing
new sanctions on Iran,

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:42.668
lied about the intelligence
that led to the assassination

00:01:42.668 --> 00:01:45.205
of Soleimani,
and then urged the world

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:47.707
to strike a new peace deal
with Iran.

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:50.376
The speech itself was
as dizzying as Trump's entrance,

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.312
when the doors opened
and he emerged from...

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:53.379
a spaceship?

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:56.415
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:58.350
[ Fresh laughter and applause ]

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.585
I mean, look at him.

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:02.655
He looks like Mr. Burns
with radiation poisoning.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:06.258
[ Applause ]

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:11.097
And, much like
the alien Mr. Burns,

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.598
Trump claimed to want peace,

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:14.934
but the whole thing was
incoherent and bizarre.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:18.271
For example, after he descended
from his blue tractor beam,

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.139
he launched into the speech

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:22.308
before he addressed
the audience.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:29.949
-As long as I'm president
of the United States,

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:35.588
Iran will never be allowed
to have a nuclear weapon.

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:36.723
Good morning.

00:02:36.723 --> 00:02:40.326
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.261
-And...good morning to you?

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:43.696
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:46.599
It'd be fun if Trump started
every conversation like that.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.534
[as Trump]
As long as I'm president,

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:52.705
Iran will never have
a nuclear weapon.

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:57.143
I'll have a Filet-O-Fish
and six Big Macs.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:59.044
And if you were thrown
off-balance

00:02:59.044 --> 00:03:00.813
by Trump's wild swings

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.082
from starting a conflict
to claiming he stopped one,

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:04.917
you are not alone because,
as usual,

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:07.119
Trump himself seemed off-kilter

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:09.489
and had trouble reading
from the teleprompter.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:13.158
-The civilized world must send
a clear and unified message

00:03:13.158 --> 00:03:15.495
to the Iranian regime.

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:18.164
Your campaign of terror,
murder, mayhem,

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:22.267
will not be toleri-- any longer.

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:24.270
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:28.507
-Yes.
[as Trump] Tolera-deh-deh.

00:03:28.507 --> 00:03:31.577
I love when he gets in trouble
halfway through a word

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:34.380
and then rather than just
stop and reboot,

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:38.717
reaches in his mind for what he
thinks the rest of the word is.

00:03:38.717 --> 00:03:41.353
[as Trump]
Tolerate. Toler-ah-deh.

00:03:41.353 --> 00:03:42.654
Toblerone.

00:03:42.654 --> 00:03:44.390
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:47.526
Trump must have been blinded
[laughing] by that blue light.

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:50.029
And it probably only got worse
when the speech ended

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.031
and Trump went back
through the doors

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.366
[ Laughter ]
and into the light again.

00:03:54.366 --> 00:03:56.636
God, it's like
that episode of "Seinfeld"

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:58.538
where a Kenny Rogers Roasters
opens

00:03:58.538 --> 00:04:00.273
right next
to Kramer's apartment.

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.374
[ Electricity humming ]

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:04.043
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:07.146
This speech swung wildly
from bluster to threats

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:09.281
to offerings of peace,
to flat-out lies.

00:04:09.281 --> 00:04:11.283
In fact, you'll never guess
who Trump blamed

00:04:11.283 --> 00:04:13.285
for the military conflict
he provoked

00:04:13.285 --> 00:04:15.321
by assassinating
a top Iranian general.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:17.456
Trump repeated
an insane talking point

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:19.125
his GOP allies and Fox pundits

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:20.659
have trotted out
since last night.

00:04:20.659 --> 00:04:22.995
They all tried to place
the blame for what happened

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:25.798
not on President Trump,
but on President Obama.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:29.168
-The missiles fired last night
at us and our allies

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:32.839
were paid for
with the funds made available

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:34.840
by the last administration.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.844
-In a very real sense,
the missiles that we saw fired

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:39.678
on US servicemen and -women
tonight

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:41.881
were paid for by the billions

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:45.218
that the Obama administration
flooded the ayatollah with.

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:47.720
-A lot of these offensive
capabilities you're seeing

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:51.057
were paid for
by Obama-Biden foreign policy.

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:53.559
-Listen -- this instant,
this moment right now,

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:56.395
is on Barack Obama,
not Donald Trump.

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:58.364
-You're blaming Obama for this?

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:00.532
First of all, he pursued
diplomacy with Iran.

00:05:00.532 --> 00:05:02.902
Second, the guy's been
out of office for three years.

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:04.737
He's been busy windsurfing,

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:06.138
whitewater rafting,
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.138 --> 00:05:09.208
and gradually unbuttoning
his shirt one button at a time.

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:11.610
[ Laughter and applause ]
In fact, Obama's shirt

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:13.946
is basically our new
threat level meter.

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.715
When he was the president
and wearing a suit,

00:05:16.715 --> 00:05:18.050
things were calm.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.386
When Trump took office
and Obama started undressing,

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:22.220
things got crazy!

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:24.723
You ever see Obama walkin'
around without a shirt on,

00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:27.125
get in a bomb shelter
immediately!

00:05:27.125 --> 00:05:28.327
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:28.327 --> 00:05:30.563
Now, needless to say,
this claim about Obama

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.498
giving Iran billions of dollars
is a lie

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.000
that has been
repeatedly debunked,

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.401
but it doesn't matter
to these guys,

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:36.903
because they're all obsessed
with Obama.

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:39.638
Now, don't get me wrong --
there's a lot you can criticize

00:05:39.638 --> 00:05:41.807
about Obama's expansion
of war powers

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:44.910
and the national security state
and his use of drones,

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:47.947
but it's insane to blame Obama
for a military conflict

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.815
with a country
he pursued peace with.

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:51.283
What's Trump gonna
blame him for next?

00:05:51.283 --> 00:05:52.718
Is Obama the one who told you

00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:55.288
to breathe in through your nose
before every word

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:57.790
like a scuba diver
about to go underwater?

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:04.196
[ Laughter ]
-[ Sniffing ]

00:06:04.196 --> 00:06:07.566
-Pssss!
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:07.566 --> 00:06:10.102
But maybe the most incoherent
part of Trump's speech

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:12.271
came at the end,
when he actually claimed

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:15.174
he wanted a deal with Iran,
despite the fact

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:17.343
that he ripped up the Obama deal

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:19.645
that multiple allies
had agreed to and that everyone,

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:21.814
even his own former
Defense Secretary James Mattis,

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:22.982
said was working.

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:25.818
-The United States
will immediately impose

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:29.922
additional punishing economic
sanctions on the Iranian regime.

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:33.258
Iran must abandon
its nuclear ambitions

00:06:33.258 --> 00:06:35.928
and end its support
for terrorism.

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:37.262
[ Sniffs ]

00:06:37.262 --> 00:06:42.335
The time has come for the
United Kingdom, Germany, France,

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:46.138
Russia, and China [sniff]
to recognize this reality.

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:49.074
[ Sniffs ]
They must now break away

00:06:49.074 --> 00:06:51.644
from the remnants
of the Iran deal,

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:56.482
and we must all work together
toward making a deal with Iran

00:06:56.482 --> 00:07:00.652
that makes the world
a safer and more peaceful place.

00:07:00.652 --> 00:07:02.421
-Oh, now you want a deal?

00:07:02.421 --> 00:07:05.657
You already ripped up one
and then attacked them.

00:07:05.657 --> 00:07:07.660
Why would they negotiate
a second deal

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:08.828
with a guy who lies
about everything

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:10.162
and always goes back
on his word?

00:07:10.162 --> 00:07:12.165
It's like if you got
one of those spam calls

00:07:12.165 --> 00:07:13.966
offering you a free cruise,

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:16.135
and then they called you again
and you were like,

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:19.271
"Okay, I'll give you my
Social Security number again,

00:07:19.271 --> 00:07:21.673
but this time, I'd better get
that trip to Hawaii.

00:07:21.673 --> 00:07:23.509
I want to go paddleboarding
with Obama.

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:25.511
Oh, God, he's shirtless!
Run!"

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:27.179
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.179 --> 00:07:29.681
This strategy of ripping up
the deal, attacking them,

00:07:29.681 --> 00:07:32.117
and then demanding a new deal
obviously makes no sense.

00:07:32.117 --> 00:07:35.587
Trump's impulsive seesawing from
conflict to threats to restraint

00:07:35.587 --> 00:07:39.158
show us why Congress must
reclaim its constitutional power

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:40.492
and stop any president,

00:07:40.492 --> 00:07:42.328
let alone a president
as deranged as Trump,

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:44.130
from unilaterally waging a war

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.965
or triggering a conflict
like this again.

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:47.466
Congress has the power
to stop this.

00:07:47.466 --> 00:07:48.500
There's a lot they can do.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.403
They can pass
a war powers resolution.

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:51.737
They can block war funding.

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:54.440
They can repeal both
Bush-era authorizations

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:55.741
for the use of military force.

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:57.810
They could even
keep Trump distracted

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.678
by tying a chicken nugget
to a Roomba

00:07:59.678 --> 00:08:01.279
and letting it loose
in the White House.

00:08:01.279 --> 00:08:03.515
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:03.515 --> 00:08:05.184
[as Trump] I can't talk
about Iran now.

00:08:05.184 --> 00:08:07.152
Where did you go?

00:08:07.152 --> 00:08:11.324
Where'd you go,
you little piece of chicken?

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:12.692
Because Trump and his allies

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:14.827
have been insisting,
in Orwellian fashion,

00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:17.696
that this act of war
was actually an attempt

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:19.698
to de-escalate and stop a war,

00:08:19.698 --> 00:08:22.568
that Trump has the power
to do whatever he wants,

00:08:22.568 --> 00:08:24.669
and also, that none of this
is his fault.

00:08:24.669 --> 00:08:28.207
But make no mistake, this
completely unnecessary crisis

00:08:28.207 --> 00:08:29.608
was entirely Trump's doing.

00:08:29.608 --> 00:08:32.378
He's been on a march toward
conflict with Iran from day one,

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:34.680
which is why Congress has to
stop this from happening again.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.682
Last year, for example,
he was asked

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:38.484
if he had an exit strategy
in mind

00:08:38.484 --> 00:08:40.286
for what would have
undoubtedly been

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:43.055
a catastrophic war with Iran,
and he admitted that he did not.

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:46.325
-Do you have an exit strategy
for Iran, if war does break out?

00:08:46.325 --> 00:08:49.128
-Uh, you're not gonna need
an exit strategy.

00:08:49.128 --> 00:08:50.396
-[Laughing]

00:08:50.396 --> 00:08:52.398
-I don't need exit strategies.

00:08:52.398 --> 00:08:54.800
-And, of course, Trump doesn't
have an exit strategy for war.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:57.136
He didn't even have
a literal exit strategy

00:08:57.136 --> 00:08:59.705
when he and Ben Carson missed
their cues at a debate,

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:01.874
got stuck in a hallway,
and just froze.

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:03.075
[ Laughter ]

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:04.776
[as Trump]
Well, this is our life now.

00:09:04.776 --> 00:09:06.778
We live in this hallway.

00:09:06.778 --> 00:09:07.913
I mean, look at them.

00:09:07.913 --> 00:09:09.582
They look like extras in a movie

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:11.951
who accidentally wandered
onto the wrong set.

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:14.586
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.586 --> 00:09:17.255
[as Trump] What's with
all these hamster people?

00:09:17.255 --> 00:09:20.092
They're cats?! [ Groans ]

00:09:20.092 --> 00:09:21.560
This movie's not gonna work.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:22.895
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.895 --> 00:09:24.563
And even when Trump does exit,

00:09:24.563 --> 00:09:25.964
he doesn't do it
with a strategy.

00:09:25.964 --> 00:09:27.466
He just wanders
aimlessly offstage

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:28.567
while other people are talking,

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:31.303
like a grandpa who's lost
at Disney World.

00:09:31.303 --> 00:09:33.739
"Disneyland?! But I wanted
to go to Fantasy Land!

00:09:33.739 --> 00:09:35.875
That's the strip club
I went to in 'Nam."

00:09:35.875 --> 00:09:37.143
[ Laughter ]

00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:39.445
Presidents of both parties
have been accumulating

00:09:39.445 --> 00:09:41.113
unconstitutional war powers
for themselves

00:09:41.113 --> 00:09:42.714
going back decades,
and of course it was

00:09:42.714 --> 00:09:44.616
a Republican president,
George W. Bush,

00:09:44.616 --> 00:09:48.153
who orchestrated an illegal
invasion of Iraq based on lies,

00:09:48.153 --> 00:09:50.522
established a secret network
of CIA black sites

00:09:50.522 --> 00:09:52.658
to carry out illegal torture,
choked on a pretzel,

00:09:52.658 --> 00:09:54.760
got stuck in a room when he
tried to open a locked door,

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:57.963
and then retired to become
the Republican Bob Ross.

00:09:57.963 --> 00:09:59.464
[ Laughter ]

00:09:59.464 --> 00:10:01.133
And, like Bush,
Trump sees himself

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:02.934
as above the law
and popular opinion.

00:10:02.934 --> 00:10:05.503
For example, you might
remember that, in 2006,

00:10:05.503 --> 00:10:06.739
amid calls for the firing

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:08.540
of Defense Secretary
Donald Rumsfeld

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.976
during the disastrous Iraq war,
Bush said this...

00:10:10.976 --> 00:10:12.979
-I have strong confidence
in Don Rumsfeld.

00:10:12.979 --> 00:10:15.481
I hear the voices
and I read the front page

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:17.416
and I know the speculation.

00:10:17.416 --> 00:10:19.551
But I'm the decider
and I decide what is best

00:10:19.551 --> 00:10:21.520
and what's best is
for Don Rumsfeld

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:23.856
to remain as the
secretary of defense.

00:10:23.856 --> 00:10:25.224
-That's right --
he's the decider.

00:10:25.224 --> 00:10:26.858
He could've just said
"decision maker,"

00:10:26.858 --> 00:10:28.127
but why mangle two words

00:10:28.127 --> 00:10:30.496
when you can combine them
into one even dumber word?

00:10:30.496 --> 00:10:31.564
[ Laughter ]

00:10:31.564 --> 00:10:33.666
"I'm the decider,
and whatever I decide,

00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:35.468
you're just gonna have
to tolera-deh-deh!"

00:10:35.468 --> 00:10:37.336
[ Laughter ]

00:10:37.336 --> 00:10:40.005
So, after orchestrating
an illegal and disastrous war

00:10:40.005 --> 00:10:42.508
in Iraq, Bush said he alone
gets to make the decisions

00:10:42.508 --> 00:10:45.277
and now Trump and his allies are
taking that logic even further.

00:10:45.277 --> 00:10:48.180
Last night on Fox News,
Senator Lindsey Graham said

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:49.681
Article II of the Constitution,

00:10:49.681 --> 00:10:51.683
which outlines the powers
of the presidency,

00:10:51.683 --> 00:10:55.054
give Trump the ability
to unilaterally attack Iran,

00:10:55.054 --> 00:10:57.489
which it does not, and Trump
himself has repeatedly insisted

00:10:57.489 --> 00:11:00.159
that Article II lets him do
literally whatever he wants.

00:11:00.159 --> 00:11:02.395
-The president has
all the authority he needs

00:11:02.395 --> 00:11:04.630
under Article II to respond

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:07.132
and how he responds
has yet to be determined,

00:11:07.132 --> 00:11:09.634
but he has that authority
to respond.

00:11:09.634 --> 00:11:12.004
-Article II allows me to do
whatever I want.

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:14.306
Nobody ever mentions Article II.

00:11:14.306 --> 00:11:16.975
It gives me all of these rights

00:11:16.975 --> 00:11:19.378
at a level that nobody
has ever seen before.

00:11:19.378 --> 00:11:21.146
We don't even talk
about Article II.

00:11:21.146 --> 00:11:22.982
[ Applause ]
Then I have an Article II,

00:11:22.982 --> 00:11:26.084
where I have the right to do
whatever I want as president,

00:11:26.084 --> 00:11:28.754
but, I don't even talk
about that.

00:11:28.754 --> 00:11:30.989
[ Laughter ]
-First of all, you're wrong.

00:11:30.989 --> 00:11:32.657
Second, saying,
"I have an Article II"

00:11:32.657 --> 00:11:35.227
sounds like how a cabbie
from Queens would say it

00:11:35.227 --> 00:11:36.895
while fighting
with a traffic cop.

00:11:36.895 --> 00:11:38.764
"Oh, you want to see my papers?
They're right here.

00:11:38.764 --> 00:11:40.766
I got a Article I
and an Article II!"

00:11:40.766 --> 00:11:41.934
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.934 --> 00:11:43.202
"There you go. I'm gonna
make 'em kiss for you.

00:11:43.202 --> 00:11:46.071
There you go."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:46.071 --> 00:11:48.740
Trump's strategy toward Iran
is incoherent and dangerous.

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:50.208
No president,
especially Donald Trump,

00:11:50.208 --> 00:11:51.910
should have the war powers
they currently have

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:53.845
and Congress should
immediately take them back

00:11:53.845 --> 00:11:55.981
and stop a crisis like this
from happening again,

00:11:55.981 --> 00:11:58.617
because another disastrous
military conflict

00:11:58.617 --> 00:12:01.153
in the Middle East is definitely
something that can't be...

00:12:01.153 --> 00:12:02.354
-Toleri--

00:12:02.354 --> 00:12:04.256
[ Laughter ]
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:04.256 --> 00:12:08.394 line:0%
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

